# Theme Color Modes

Token **names** differ per theme. This rule is the shared **mode → semantic children** contract. Discover exact class and variable names from **this repo’s `_styles/`** before writing markup. Names in this file are **illustrative** — replace them with what `_styles/` actually defines.

## Two layers

1. **Primitives / brand scales** — raw ramps in theme CSS (often `--color-<brand>-*`). Define the palette only. Never emit them as Liquid Tailwind classes.
2. **Semantic roles** — background, text, and border utilities the theme maps onto those primitives (often `bg-surface`, `text-primary`, `border-secondary` **or this theme’s equivalents**). These are the only color utilities allowed in Liquid.

## Mode first

1. Read the Figma / schema tone (`primary` | `secondary` | `muted` | `accent` | `contrast` | `elevated`, or whatever this theme names).
2. Grep `_styles/` for `@utility`, `color-schema-*`, or the theme’s equivalent mode classes.
3. Put the matching mode class on the **section root** (or the wrapper this theme documents).
4. Children use **only semantic utilities**. The mode remaps those tokens — do not restyle children with primitives or hex to “match Figma.”

If this theme has a separate **brand vertical** axis (e.g. `education` | `industrial`), treat it the same way: one root class discovered from `_styles/`, children stay semantic.

## Size modes

Breakpoint / density modes (`lg` | `md` | `default`, or this theme’s names) map to **responsive utilities** (`md:`, `lg:`) and theme size tokens — never hard `px` or `text-[14px]`.

## Forbidden

- Arbitrary hex / rgb in Tailwind: `text-[#d1d1d1]`, `bg-[#fff]`, `border-[rgb(...)]`
- Inventing token or utility names that do not exist in `_styles/`
- Building class names with Liquid: `text-{{ color }}`, `bg-{{ settings.color }}`
- Primitive / brand-scale classes in Liquid

## Discovery (do this before coding)

```bash
rg -n "@utility|color-schema|--background-color|--text-color|--border-color|@theme" _styles/
```

Typical homes (paths vary by theme): `_styles/02_base/*colors*.css`, `_styles/01_theme/*primitives*.css`, `_styles/main.css`.

Then read `tailwindcss-rules.mdc` (static classes, `@source`) and `figma-design-system.mdc` (Figma → Liquid).

## Illustrative only

```liquid
<section class="color-schema-muted">
  <div class="bg-surface text-primary border-secondary">
    <h2 class="text-primary">…</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary">…</p>
  </div>
</section>
```

`color-schema-muted`, `bg-surface`, and `text-primary` are examples. Replace them with utilities this theme defines in `_styles/`.
